2
Product Defaults
PrDefs

This table used to be an extension (inheritance) of Prods, that is, it contained exactly the same fields. This turned out to be the wrong way of modeling the PDefs table because, for starters, these tables have different primary key (PrID\\
 for Prods and PrType for PDefs). There are also other differences between these tables:\
\
- PrNum is not a field of PDefs, while is an alternate key on Prods.\
- PDefs does not keep track of TxNum, SMNum, NFNum, or NtNum.\
- Even when PDefs does keep track of ClNum and the label links (LbNum1, LbNum2, and LbNum3), semantically there is no relationship between PDefs table and Classes and Labels tables.\
\
In light of this, I modeled the PDefs table independently from the Prods table, although any changes to the latter will likely cause a change to the former.\
\
In order to reduce the duplication of fields as much as possible (otherwise one may not get updated when the other is updated), most of the common fields were added to a PCommon table that is not generated into the database. The memo and\\
 checksum fields were not added to this table because they are supposed to be put at the end of each table and the inheritance mechanism within this tool puts the inherited fields at the top of each table.

